From: Austin Schuh <austin.linux@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] r8169: re-enable interrupt source RxOverflow

This reverts commit 6994520a3328 ("r8169: disable interrupt source
RxOverflow") for the chips it changed.

That commit reasoned that running out of RX descriptors always comes with
NAPI already being scheduled.  On an RTL8168h (XID 541) behind a Tegra234
DesignWare root port, receiving at line rate from a TSO sender, it doesn't:
NAPI runs, finds no RX work, completes and unmasks, and the chip then
latches RxOverflow (RxDescUnavail) | RxFIFOOver | TxDescUnavail with none
of them in IntrMask.  No MSI ever comes, TX stops with NPQ still set in
TxPoll, and the link is dead until the TX watchdog resets the chip 5 s
later.  Captured three times with IntrMask 0x002f, IntrStatus 0x00d0.

With RxOverflow in the mask the chip interrupts on it, the handler acks
the latched status and schedules NAPI, and RX resumes.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8169_main.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8169_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8169_main.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8169_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8169_main.c
@@ -5108,6 +5108,8 @@ static void rtl_set_irq_mask(struct rtl8169_private *tp)

 	if (tp->mac_version <= RTL_GIGA_MAC_VER_06)
 		tp->irq_mask |= SYSErr | RxFIFOOver;
+	else
+		tp->irq_mask |= RxOverflow;
 }

 static int rtl_alloc_irq(struct rtl8169_private *tp)
--
2.47.0
